About Ogilvy &nbsp;

Ogilvy, part of WPP, has been creating impact for brands through iconic, culture-changing, value-driving ideas since the company was founded by David Ogilvy 75 years ago. It builds on that rich legacy through Borderless Creativity - innovating at the intersections of its advertising, public relations, relationship design, consulting, and health capabilities with experts collaborating seamlessly across over 120 offices in nearly 90 countries. Ogilvy currently ranks as the #1 global agency network for creative excellence and effectiveness by WARC, signifying its ability to deliver creative solutions that drive unreasonable impact for clients and communities. Ogilvy is a WPP company (NYSE: WPP). For more information, visit  Ogilvy.com , and follow us on LinkedIn ,  X ,  Instagram , and Facebook.

&nbsp;

About WPP

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. We unite&nbsp;cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, world-class creativity, next-generation production, transformative enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel&nbsp;in a single company -&nbsp;powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open,&nbsp;to help our clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit&nbsp; WPP.com .

Business unit:  Ogilvy One (WPP Enterprise Solutions)

Team: Design

Location:   Auckland &nbsp;

Employment type: Permanent

&nbsp;

ABOUT THE ROLE

&nbsp;

The Digital Designer is a key member of the Ogilvy One design team, responsible for producing high-quality, on-brand digital assets across web, social media, EDM, and app channels. This role&nbsp;sits within the Ogilvy One&nbsp;New Zealand&nbsp;team and works&nbsp;closely with&nbsp;the CX + Digital Director and Digital Project Director&nbsp;to bring&nbsp;XD&nbsp;and CX experiences&nbsp;to life with strong craft, consistency, and attention to detail. &nbsp;

The role will also offer the chance to collaborate with the UX/CX team in Australia, allowing this person to work together, learn, and develop their skills within a supportive team environment. &nbsp;

The ideal candidate is a confident mid-level designer who can execute across multiple formats, contribute ideas, respond well to feedback, and continue to grow their craft in a fast-paced agency environment. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

WHAT YOU'LL DO

&nbsp;

• Create on-brand digital assets across websites, landing pages, social media, EDMs, display formats, and app experiences using Figma and Adobe Creative Cloud.

• Translate briefs, brand guidelines, campaign ideas, and UX requirements into polished design solutions that are fit for purpose and channel-ready.

• Collaborate to develop work, build capability, and ensure output aligns to team standards and creative expectations.

• Work with CX, UX, copywriters, developers, and production teams to deliver work accurately and on time.

• Adapt and resize creative and content across channels and formats while maintaining consistency, brand integrity, and design quality.

• Support concept development through layouts, mock-ups, components, design systems, and presentation-ready visuals.

• Prepare organised design files, prototypes, and handover assets that support smooth review and production workflows.

• Participate in internal and client reviews, take feedback constructively, and refine work to meet requirements.

• Stay current with digital design trends, platform specifications, and emerging AI-enabled tools that support better workflow and craft. &nbsp;

• Strong organisational skills, the ability to manage multiple tasks, and a high standard of file hygiene and detail. &nbsp;

• Clear communication skills and a collaborative mindset when working with cross-functional teams and stakeholders. &nbsp;

• A willingness to explore and use AI responsibly to support ideation, production efficiency, and the design process where&nbsp; appropriate

&nbsp;

WHAT YOU'L

Category: IT Services

Location:

For an international project in Washington, we are urgently looking for a Senior .NET / API Developer with Azure experience. Candidates need to be available within 2 to 4 weeks!

We are looking for a contractor, who is able to work 8 hours US (Washington) time. This position is long-term. Candidates need to be fluent in English.

Profile:

• Bachelor or Master degree;

• +8 years of .NET development experience;

• Experience of programming and scripting languages/frameworks such as .NET core, .NET, ASP.net, .NET Frameworks;

• Experience of range services from the Microsoft Azure Cloud Platform including Infrastructure and Security related services such as Azure AD, IaaS, PaaS, Containers, Storage, Azure Monitoring, Security, App Insights and Log Analytics;

• Experience on Microsoft Azure Platform as A Service (PaaS) products such as Azure SQL, AppService, Logic Apps, Functions, Azure App Services, APIM and other Serverless services.

• Experience with claims-based authentication (SAML/OAuth/OIDC), MFA and RBAC;

• Evident hands-on experience with one or more of serverless architecture (Azure Functions), Azure API Management, Middleware (Azure Service bus), Azure Event Hub, Azure Batch, Azure App Services;

• Good understanding of Microsoft Identity and Access Management products such including Azure AD AD B2C;

• Good understanding of Azure cloud service offering (covering Azure Compute, Storage, Network, WebApp, Azure Cognitive Services, Azure Functions, Azure AD);

• Knowledge of PowerShell, Git, ARM templates and deployment automation using Azure DevOps;

• Knowledge on Azure Data Lake, Azure DevOps / Databases like Redis, Cosmos DB and Web service integration;

• Knowledge on Open API standards, ODATA interfaces;

• Good knowledge of quality standards, security, and best practice;

• Working knowledge on Azure DevOps and ability to interpret the results of code coverage and security scans and create remediation plans;

• Demonstrated deep engineering and development expertise on Microsoft Azure PAAS, FAAS and IAAS stack of services;

• Designed high performance, scalable and secure cloud native and hybrid cloud applications, APIs and Microservices with .NET Core and Microsoft Azure PAAS, Functions-as-a-Services;

• Understanding of Identity management and modern authentication and authorization protocols such as OIDC, OAuth 2.0 using Azure Active Directory;

• Understanding of CI/CD and continuous testing practices with Azure DevOps into the engineering lifecycle;

• Fluent in English;

